cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Astro Canvas in work you publish, please cite it.
title: 'Astro Canvas: a node-based infinite canvas for astronomical data'
abstract: >-
  Astro Canvas is a node-based infinite canvas for exploring astronomical spectra, images and
  integral-field cubes. A reactive execution engine runs a workflow document as a directed graph
  with content-hash caching, cost gating and cancellation; a browser canvas builds itself from the
  node schemas the server publishes; and the science lives in installable node packs. The first
  packs rebuild the rbcodes analysis GUIs (equivalent widths, redshift finding, multi-spectrum line
  identification and IFU cube tools) as headless, composable nodes, so the same measurement can be
  made interactively, run over a table of targets, or executed from a shell with no display.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-05'
license: MIT
